<title>LEBANON: Lebanon wants customs agents, employees jailed.</title>
<headline>Lebanon wants customs agents, employees jailed.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Lebanese prosecutor filed on Monday charges carrying at least five years in jail against 20 customs agents and employees accusing them of forgery and bribery, judicial sources said.</p>
<p>Prosecutor Abdallah Bitar said the suspects who included 11 state employees were accused of bribery and &quot;forging hundreds of thousands of customs documents&quot; to exempt some traders from paying duties on imported goods, the sources said.</p>
<p>Fifteen of the suspects have already been detained.  Bitar ordered the arrest of the remaining five.</p>
</text>
